 "input": "Why squares, and not plain sizes? Because squares add up over perpendicular pieces. That is Pythagoras: the square on the long side equals the two squares on the short sides. Fourier analysis obeys the same law. Split a signal into waves, and its energy equals the total energy of the waves. That is Parseval’s identity, and it is why physicists call the integral of a signal squared its energy. The word stuck.",
